A||N||9||bHooper||if Pontiac refuses to build it, maybe Saturn will!||||10||
Z||000000||bHooper||02-17-2001||07:53 PM||||yesterday i walked into a Saturn dealership for the first time (to pick up manifold studs for the fiero).  i felt real comfortable... especially when they had a car with the body removed, revealing the space frame.<P>while waiting for the kid behind the counter to get my order together, i had a moment of briliance... "<B>wouldn't it be a great fit, for Saturn to build a mid-engine sportscar with a plastic, spaceframe body?</B>"<P>so, i asked the cashier if they had a suggestion box.  she said to go to <A HREF="http://www.saturn.com" TARGET=_blank>www.saturn.com</A>  and email them.<P>so, i did... and here is what they said: <I>Dear Brian,<P>Thanks for writing Saturn.  I would love to see Saturn offer a sports <BR>car!  It would be fantastic;<BR>however, I am not aware of any plans to do this in the future.  We can <BR>tell you that Saturn is<BR>considering a number of future products--all of which may or may not <BR>make it to market.  Stay<BR>tuned...as always, we will communicate with our customers at the right <BR>time if we are introducing<BR>new products.<P>Thanks again,<P>Sheron Hobgood<BR>Saturn Customer Assistance Center<BR>qveh/ttd</I><P>maybe everyone should go to Saturns website and email them?!  it's obvious that 12 years of wining to Pontiac has done little to advance our cause, so lets try another outlet.  who knows, maybe one of these days someone will decide to build something to compete with Toyota, Honda, Nissan (new Z), Mazda, BMW, and Porsche!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings<p>[This message has been edited by bHooper (edited 02-17-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||Hank is Here||02-17-2001||08:28 PM||||Saturn is a good car company but I wouldn't want them to build a sports  car.  The fact of the matter is that if you look at the orginoal Saturn Cars in 1991 and look at new ons they appear simliar, I think that state of no or little change would be boring.  I am enjoying what I have, sure it would be great if another car like it was built but I wouldn't count on it.  Heck if I had the dough I'd see about importing one of those Speedsters||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||02-17-2001||08:56 PM||||I think the Saturns are built in the same plant where the Fieros were made. It really irritates me when I hear someone bragging about how their Saturn has un-dentable body panels. Why does Saturn get all the credit for being the first to do that?<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000003||Tigger||02-17-2001||09:19 PM||||The Saturn plant is in Springhill Tenn. and the new LS's are being made in Wilmington Delaware.<P>Not the same plant, however lots of engineers and designers of the Fiero were put on the original Saturn team.<P>Basically you got the "We thank you for your interest, we are looking to market new vehicles however SUV's and wagons are the big thing right now." response.  It was worth a shot.  I think I'll write them too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||02-17-2001||10:36 PM||||ya never ever know!<P>if 1980 people emailed em, maybe the would start to think about it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierosound||02-17-2001||10:46 PM||||I got this latest "news" from alt.autos.camaro.firebird newsgroup<P>"There has been more rumors flying out of GMs doors than anyone knows what to do with. First the demise of the camaro and Firebird then the demise of the Oldsmobile line.<P>The latest tops them all. As rumor has it, the Pontiac line is going to re-introduce the Fiero. <P>According to the alligations there will be three versions avalable, The Base form will be a the Fiero G2, which will be available with the Generation 2(hence the name G2) V6 w/ 4 speed auto or 5-speed manual. The other 2 forms will be. The Fiero F1 (Formula 1) and<BR>Fiero SS. <P>Tell me why this seems suspiciously like the Firebird. The F1 and SS will both be available with The LS1 (????) and will both be available with the famous WS6 Perfomance Upgrade. According to GM the F1  will be the only form available with a removabe top and will have head rest roll bars where as the SS is only available w/the basic T-top.<P>The F1 and SS have either 4spd Auto or a six manual. The WS6 will have the Ram Air the tighter suspension 17x9.5 front and 17x11 back. The car is suposidly going to look like it used to except more agressive and<BR>extremely updated.  The Biggest difference from the old is that this one is said to have a tranversly mounted engine. <P>According to experts it is going to out handle the Firebird, Camaro, and Mustang and will have almost the same wheelbase as before. And to top it off, if it is released, the price will compete with the Mustang. (I find that hard to believe). In Fact I find this whole thing hard to swallow, considering the Fireos history.<P>But if They have the Balls to do this I will be really interseted to see exactly what happens with it. I was wondering if anyone else got the same E-mail I did. I was also wondering if anyone knows if this is just crap or if its true. we'll see..."<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000006||pHoOl||02-18-2001||10:42 AM||||I've had both a saturn and now a fiero.  I have heard that the fiero has enduraflex body panels or something of the sort.  I kinda witnessed this when sliding into a mailbox, seeing the front facia crunch up and bend right back out after i hit reverse.<P>However, I still would not take a baseball bat to my fiero like i did with the saturn to prove the flex panels.<P>Also, as for the comment about the body style not changing.... They have made body style changes every two years since 94.  Some of them are subtle, others more obvious (95 to 96 sedans).  I think that they've done a good job changing it up.  And i don't think that they look any more similar to the original car than any others.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||LZeitgeist||02-18-2001||11:48 AM||||"Hank is Here" wrote:<BR>"Saturn is a good car company but I wouldn't want them to build a sports car. The fact of the matter is that if you look at the orginoal Saturn Cars in 1991 and look at new ons they appear simliar, I think that state of no or little change would be boring."<P><BR>That's a pretty ironic statement, considering that with a Fiero, you can remove any and/or all of the body panels from the first year of production and install them on a chassis from the last year of production...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 02-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||02-18-2001||12:47 PM||||Just for the record, Saturn is the same group of people who designed and built the Fiero. The Fiero plant in Michigan was owned by the employee's. When GM axed the Fiero, The management team was offered Saturn. But the management team negotiated the contract so they had total control where The Fiero project they had restrictions. (GM controlled what parts they could use and all the funding for advertisement, which is how GM killed the Fiero. They cut the advertising budget by 70% and the deal was they had to sell 30,000 Fiero's per year to remain open.) Anyhow, Saturn grabbed one of the 3 machines that was used to make the Fiero and built the Saturn cars with the same "enduraflex" panels. GM kept the other 2 machines to make panels for the vans (Lumina, trans sport, stilletto). When GM started making the vans out of metal a few years back, Saturn sucked up the other 2 machines. Hence we now have the LS series Saturns. The 3rd machine isn't in use....Yet.<BR>The second machine is being used to make the SUV panels too. Both Pontiac and Saturn have expressed intrest in the Opel Speedster but lately there isn't any new rumors about that.<BR>(I know someone who works at the Saturn plant) So in effect Saturn is a cousin of the Fiero. <P>As for the rumors of the Fiero (G2,F1,SS) are what is being reported, It would most likely be a Corvette status car. In other words high $$$. The rumors say it will competitive to price as the Mustang, But which Mustang? the Cobra? Your probabluy looking at a $30,000 + car if it ever happens. (which I doubt since GM has tried too many times to bury the Fiero name. In fact it's not even listed in the Pontiac Historical site.)||||reg||1
Z||000009||Pontiaddict||02-18-2001||03:44 PM||||GM screwed Saturn over too. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.autoextremist.com/archives/990706/index.shtml" TARGET=_blank>http://www.autoextremist.com/archives/990706/index.shtml</A> <P>It also mentions the Fiero.||||reg||1
